Deputy Kovacs, played by Jeff Goldblum.

11
00:39:17,142 --> 00:39:23,142
The Grand Budapest Hotel is a 2014 comedy-drama film
written and directed by Wes Anderson.

12
00:42:51,428 --> 00:42:57,428
The film's seventeen-actor ensemble cast is led by Ralph Fiennes as Monsieur Gustave H., famed
concierge of a twentieth-century mountainside resort in the fictional country of Zubrowka.

13
00:46:25,714 --> 00:46:31,714
After being framed for the murder of a wealthy dowager (Tilda Swinton), he and his recently befriended protégé Zero (Tony Revolori)
embark on a quest for fortune and a priceless Renaissance painting amidst the backdrop of an encroaching fascist regime.

14
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
Anderson's American Empirical Pictures produced the film in association with Studio Babelsberg,
Fox Searchlight Pictures, and Indian Paintbrush's Scott Rudin and Steven Rales.

15
00:53:34,285 --> 00:53:40,285
Fox Searchlight supervised the commercial distribution, and The Grand Budapest Hotel's
funding came from Indian Paintbrush and German government-funded tax rebates.

16
00:57:08,571 --> 00:57:14,571
Anderson and longtime collaborator Hugo Guinness conceived The Grand Budapest Hotel as
a fragmented tale following a character inspired by a mutual friend.

17
01:00:42,857 --> 01:00:48,857
They initially struggled in brainstorming, but the experience touring Europe and researching the
literature of Austrian novelist Stefan Zweig shaped their vision for the film.

18
01:04:17,142 --> 01:04:23,142
The Grand Budapest Hotel draws visually from Europe-set mid-century Hollywood films and the
United States Library of Congress's photochrom print collection of alpine resorts.

19
01:07:51,428 --> 01:07:57,428
Filming took place in eastern Germany from January to March 2013.

20
01:11:25,714 --> 01:11:31,714
The film's soundtrack was composed by French composer Alexandre Desplat, incorporating symphonic
and Russian folk-inspired elements and expanding on his earlier work with Anderson.

21
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
It explores themes of fascism, nostalgia, friendship, and loyalty, and further
discourse analyze the function of color as a storytelling device.

22
01:18:34,285 --> 01:18:40,285
The Grand Budapest Hotel premiered in competition at the 64th
Berlin International Film Festival on February 6, 2014.

23
01:22:08,571 --> 01:22:14,571
It was released in theaters in March to highly positive reviews, and grossed $174.6
million worldwide at the box office, becoming Anderson's highest-grossing film.

24
01:25:42,857 --> 01:25:48,857
It was nominated for nine awards at the 87th Academy Awards including Best
Picture, winning four, and received numerous other accolades.

25
01:29:17,142 --> 01:29:23,142
Since its release, The Grand Budapest Hotel has been assessed as one
of the greatest films of the twenty-first century.

26
01:32:51,428 --> 01:32:57,428
The film explores themes of hotel, painting, wartime, eastern europe, author.

27
01:36:25,714 --> 01:36:31,714
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
